Migration strategy — zero downtime
The safest approach is run both in parallel, migrate workloads, then disable Auto Mode. Never disable Auto Mode before node groups are ready and workloads are running.

Phase 1: Prepare IAM
Phase 2: Create node groups (alongside Auto Mode)
Phase 3: Install required addons
Phase 4: Migrate workloads to node groups
Phase 5: Disable Auto Mode
Phase 6: Verify

Phase 1 — Create the node IAM role
Auto Mode uses AmazonEKSAutoNodeRole. Node groups need a separate AmazonEKSNodeRole with different policies:

# Step 1 — Create the trust policy document
cat > node-trust-policy.json << 'EOF'
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": { "Service": "ec2.amazonaws.com" },
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
  }]
}
EOF

# Step 2 — Create the role
aws iam create-role \
  --role-name AmazonEKSNodeRole \
  --assume-role-policy-document file://node-trust-policy.json

# Step 3 — Attach all 4 required policies
aws iam attach-role-policy --role-name AmazonEKSNodeRole \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy

aws iam attach-role-policy --role-name AmazonEKSNodeRole \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy

aws iam attach-role-policy --role-name AmazonEKSNodeRole \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly

aws iam attach-role-policy --role-name AmazonEKSNodeRole \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore

# Step 4 — Verify
aws iam list-attached-role-policies --role-name AmazonEKSNodeRole

