Phase 5 — Disable Auto Mode
Only do this after all pods are Running on node group nodes:

# Disable Auto Mode compute and storage
aws eks update-cluster-config \
  --name eks \
  --compute-config '{"enabled": false}' \
  --kubernetes-network-config '{"elasticLoadBalancing": {"enabled": false}}' \
  --storage-config '{"blockStorage": {"enabled": false}}' \
  --region us-east-1

# Watch the update
aws eks describe-cluster --name eks \
  --query 'cluster.status' --region us-east-1

# Verify Auto Mode node pools are gone
kubectl get nodeclaims 2>/dev/null || echo "NodeClaims API gone — Auto Mode fully disabled"

Run in CloudShell
⚠️ After disabling Auto Mode's built-in load balancing, install the AWS Load Balancer Controller via Helm if you use Ingress or LoadBalancer services — otherwise your services will lose their ALB/NLB.

# Install AWS Load Balancer Controller (replaces Auto Mode's built-in ELB)
helm repo add eks https://aws.github.io/eks-charts
helm install aws-load-balancer-controller eks/aws-load-balancer-controller \
  --namespace kube-system \
  --set clusterName=eks \
  --set serviceAccount.annotations."eks\.amazonaws\.com/role-arn"=<IRSA-role-arn>

